{"version":1,"projection":".$mem","views":{"storage":"Memory of the Rust value/place itself. Available on API value terms, Rust fields and sequence elements, including opaque generic values. It is not the pointee memory of a pointer.","region":"A typed logical region designating exactly one pointee value. Obtained as p.$mem.pointee for a raw pointer or explicitly supported pointer wrapper. Constructing this observation does not dereference the pointer and remains possible for null/dangling/misaligned pointers.","allocation":"The originating allocation record, retained after deallocation. Identity includes allocation generation, so address reuse does not establish identity."},"fields":{"exists":{"type":"bool","meaning":"Whether the view has represented backing storage. start/size/align observations do not by themselves imply this flag."},"start":{"type":"integer","meaning":"Byte address of this view's beginning. For p.$mem it is the address of the pointer slot; for p.$mem.pointee it is the pointer's data address, including 0 for null."},"size":{"type":"integer","meaning":"Byte size of the view's type: pointer-slot size for p.$mem, sizeof(T) for the region designated by *const T/*mut T. DST views use the full dynamic size. Nonnegative; never the containing allocation's capacity."},"end":{"type":"integer","meaning":"start + size on mathematical integers, without machine wrapping."},"align":{"type":"integer","meaning":"Positive byte alignment REQUIRED by the view's type, not proof that start satisfies it. Proper alignment is start % align == 0, also when size is zero."},"readable":{"type":"bool","meaning":"The whole size-byte view is valid for reads in the current state, respecting allocation provenance, liveness, range containment and access permission. Does not imply alignment or initialized/valid contents. Zero-byte read access is vacuous."},"writable":{"type":"bool","meaning":"The whole size-byte view is valid for writes in the current state, respecting allocation p